+# The Daily Grind
+
+Run the security checks with `npm test` (no server required).
+
+`message-security.mjs` configures the trusted ordering origin as
+`https://orders.thedailygrind.com`. Set `ORDERING_ORIGIN` to the real service's
+exact origin when deploying. Ordering messages use these payloads:
+
+- `{ type: 'order:redirect', url: '/thanks' }`: navigation within the page's
+  exact origin (including scheme and port).
+- `{ type: 'order:external-link', url: 'https://example.com/' }`: HTTPS links
+  without embedded credentials, opened with `noopener,noreferrer`.
+
+URLs are parsed with `URL`, rather than splitting strings or matching domain
+substrings. Outbound page anchors receive the same external-link checks.
+
+The sandboxed ordering widget sends `widget:init` before `widget:status`
+(`text`) or `widget:resize` (`height`, an integer from 40 to 600). The parent
+requires both the opaque `null` origin and the known iframe's `contentWindow`,
+then pins that sender for subsequent messages. A different sandboxed iframe
+cannot initialize or replace that identity. Widget status uses `textContent`.
